 "notes": "Top street prints 'WOOLPER' (x~6500) and 'STREET' (x~8950) on the same street; recorded as 'Woolper Street' to match the list in INSTRUCTIONS22 - check against the neighbouring strip. Woolper meets Vine as two offset T's: west leg (9500,113) and east leg stub (9466,168). 'Prospect' is printed with no suffix; it runs east from Brookline and turns south into Terrace (label 'TERRACE' only, Avenue assumed); the turn is recorded as intersection Prospect/Terrace Avenue (name change). 'W. NIXON' printed with no suffix, recorded as West Nixon Street. Hosea Avenue meets Brookline twice (offset T's): east part (7894,3473), west part (7900,3598). Vine Street junction complex at the top of Bishop: Glenmary curves south-east into the open junction where Vine (from the north, curving east), Bishop (south-south-west) and Ruther (south-east) all meet; picks Glenmary/Bishop, Glenmary/Vine and Ruther/Vine are the best centreline reads of that junction. Ludlow Avenue continues as Jefferson Avenue at the Brookline junction: Ludlow/Brookline (7965,4295) and Ludlow/Jefferson (7995,4295) are the same junction read on each centreline. Bishop Street: from Glenmary south, curves east past Marion, runs straight south at x~9100, turns south-west at Loretta Street, crosses Jefferson and runs south at x~8887 to the plate edge. Unnamed: 20 ft lane east of Biddle (continues Interwood Avenue east from the Biddle junction along y~1300, curves north, dead end at y~702); the street south of West Nixon at x~9261 whose name is cut by the plate edge ('...IAL'). Vine's east edge is the plate edge from y~300 to y~2450; Vine centre taken from the west face plus half the 60 ft width (streetcar tracks sit slightly east of centre). The diagonal line between Vine/Ruther and Marmet Street (9180,2790)-(9550,3470) is a rear lot line with a subdivision name, not a street. Not picked (beyond ~300 px east): Marmet/Bear (~9640,3930), West Nixon/Jefferson (~9640,6500), Marmet's north end."
}